==Trivia==
*This sub-chapter's name is a reference to [[wikipedia:Disneyland|Disneyland]]. Fittingly, some of its stages are parodies of real theme park attractions:
**[[50 Degrees Hotter]]'s Japanese name, Plus 50-do no Sekai (プラス50度の世界, "World of Plus 50 Degrees"), is a reference to Minus 30-do no Sekai (マイナス３０度の世界, "World of Minus 30 Degrees"), the tagline of [https://www.greenland.co.jp/park/attraction/iceworld/ Ice World], an attraction at Japanese amusement parks such as Cosmo World and Kijima Kogen Park.
**[[Irresistable Henhouse]]'s Japanese name, Yūneku no Chikin Rūmu (誘惑のチキンルーム, Irresistible Chicken Room), is most likely a reference to Disneyland's [[wikipedia:Walt Disney's Enchanted Tiki Room|Enchanted Tiki Room]], which is called Miwaku no Chiki Rūmu (魅惑のチキルーム) in Japanese.
***It may also be a reference to [https://coasterpedia.net/wiki/Chicken_exit chicken exits], where guests can exit a ride's queue line should they "chicken out" of going on the ride.
**[[The Haunted 1LDK]] is a parody of [[wikipedia:The Haunted Mansion|The Haunted Mansion]] at Disneyland. A 1LDK is a term for a simple apartment that consists solely of the 3 most important rooms: the living room, dining room and kitchen, thus creating the acronym L-D-K.
***In the changelog for [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] [[Version 5.10 Update|Version 5.10]], the sub-chapter was quite literally referred to as Disneyland.
*Mouseyland's Japanese name (ふくろのねずみランド, ''Fukuro no Nezumirando'', "No Way Out from Mouseyland") is a play on 袋のネズミ ''fukuro no nezumi'', which translates to "mouse/rat in a bag", but is an idiom meaning "trapped with no way of escape".
*In the Taiwanese version of the game, the name of this sub-chapter is 迪死你樂園, and the Taiwanese/Chinese of Disneyland is 迪士尼樂園, which is only two words off from the sub-chapter's name, where 死 means death and 你 means you, 死你 is basically (noun/verb) kills you.
**Additionally, 死你 sounds very similar to 士尼 in Mandarin.
*[[The Haunted 1LDK]] is the only Stories of Legend stage to include monthly [[:Category:Event Enemies|event enemies]] ([[Ghost Doge]], [[Ghost Snache]] and [[Ghost Baa Baa]]).

